=== AI-OFF CONTRACT ===

ADR-015 invariant evidence (only invariants this slice touches):

I1 (default-off):
  PASS — fresh DB defaults remain ai_mode='off'. The only schema
         change adds an `ai_features_archived='{}'::jsonb` row.
         No defaults flipped to true.
  EVIDENCE: migrations/000202 inserts an EMPTY archive map; F0's
            ai_mode default of 'off' is unchanged; settingsDefaults
            in settings_repo.go still seeds AIMode="off",
            AIFeatures=empty, AIProviderConfig=nil.

I3 (baseline intact):
  PASS — Settings page non-AI sections (General, Appearance,
         Advanced, Reset, link cards) untouched. The only edit to
         SettingsPage.tsx is inserting <section id="ai"> between
         appearance and advanced, plus a 5th import.
  EVIDENCE: git diff web/src/features/settings/pages/SettingsPage.tsx
            shows only an import addition and a single section
            insertion; no removals.

I4 (zero egress in off mode):
  PASS — Validate endpoint refuses to call any network path when
         mode='off' (returns 400 immediately) and refuses entirely
         when mode='cloud' beyond a no-op OK. Local-mode validation
         resolves the URL through ValidateLocalCtx which forbids
         public IPs and rejects DNS rebinding mixed-resolution.
  EVIDENCE: TestAISettingsValidateHandler_OffMode_Rejected (400);
            TestAISettingsValidateHandler_Cloud_NoOp (200, no
            outbound call asserted by handler shape — cloud branch
            returns immediately without invoking any client);
            TestAISettingsValidateHandler_LocalPublicIPLiteral_Rejected
            (422 + code=not_local).

I5 (hidden UI):
  N/A — Settings page is the OPT-IN surface and must always render
        so the user has a stable place to discover + enable AI.
        We deliberately do NOT wrap AISettings in withAiFeature().

I6 (404 routes preserved):
  PRESERVED — No new route was added under /api/v1/ai/*. The
              validate endpoint lives at /api/v1/settings/ai/* —
              that subtree is settings-namespace, not
              ai-namespace, and is invisible to the aiGuard 404
              policy by design.
  EVIDENCE: aivet still passes (output: "OK — 2 AI route(s), 2
            feature(s) in registry, TS mirror in sync"). No new
            aiGuard mounts, so the F0/F1 404 policy holds.

I7 (per-feature opt-in; no silent restore):
  PASS — (a) Per-feature toggles are generated by mapping over
            AI_FEATURE_IDS in AIFeatureToggleList — never
            hand-listed. Adding a feature to the Go registry +
            running aigen will surface it here automatically.
         (b) Mode→off transitions clear ai_features (both server
            via applyAIArchiveOnModeFlip and client via
            handleModeChange) and archive the prior selection.
         (c) Re-enabling a mode does NOT auto-restore. The user
            sees an explicit "Restore previous selection?" panel
            with separate Confirm and Decline buttons. Decline
            dismisses for the session; Confirm reifies the
            archive AND saves immediately so the archive is
            cleared on the round-trip.
  EVIDENCE: TestApplyAIArchiveOnModeFlip_LocalToOff_Archives
            (server clears + archives);
            TestApplyAIArchiveOnModeFlip_LocalToOff_EmptyPrior_NoArchive
            (no archive when nothing was on);
            TestApplyAIArchiveOnModeFlip_DefensiveClone (mutating
            the source after the call cannot leak); AISettings
            "renders one toggle row per AI_FEATURE_IDS entry"
            (UI loop is generative); AISettings "shows the
            restore panel ... Both Confirm AND Decline are
            rendered" + "hides the restore panel once the user
            declines" (no auto-restore code path exists).

I9 (key never displayed in off mode):
  PASS — (a) Server-side: settings_handler.Get nils
            AIProviderConfig (which contains the key) when
            ai_mode='off'. F0 already established this; F2 does
            not regress it.
         (b) Client-side: AISettings useEffect explicitly
            initialises api_key to '' when serverMode==='off'
            even though the server already redacts. Belt + braces.
         (c) The API key Input is type="password" with no
            defaultValue when entering cloud mode from off; the
            placeholder hints "leave blank to keep current".
  EVIDENCE: AISettings test "does not pre-populate the API key
            field when mode flips to cloud" — asserts
            apiKey.type === 'password' AND apiKey.value === '';
            settings_handler.Get test coverage from F0 still
            passes (`go test ./internal/api/...` exit 0).

I10 (type system / aivet):
  PASS — aivet exit 0 (no new /api/v1/ai/* routes were added
         outside the guard.Wrap surface). The validate endpoint
         is settings-namespace, not ai-namespace.
  EVIDENCE: `go run ./tools/aivet` → "OK — 2 AI route(s), 2
            feature(s) in registry, TS mirror in sync" (the same
            two routes F1 mounted; no new ai/* paths).

